# Centralised App Assets (Common Assets)

## Core Principle
All app assets (fonts, graphics, icons) served from single centralized location shared across Noble Architecture applications. Assets are static files on GitHub Pages, loaded dynamically via the **AssetLoader module** using absolute URLs.

## Hard Constraints
- **Read-Only at runtime** - GitHub Pages serves static content only
- Never duplicate assets into individual app directories
- **Always use AssetLoader module** for asset URL resolution
- Asset loading must work identically in local and production environments

---

# Asset Loader Module

## Unified Asset Loading System
The `CommonUtils__AssetLoader__.js` module provides centralized asset URL resolution, eliminating CORS issues and ensuring consistent asset loading across environments.

### Key Features
- **Automatic URL Resolution** - Converts asset references to absolute GitHub Pages URLs
- **Dynamic Font Loading** - Injects `@font-face` rules at runtime with absolute paths
- **Data Attribute Injection** - Reads `data-asset-src` and `data-asset-href` attributes, injects absolute URLs
- **Prevents 404 Errors** - Browser doesn't attempt to load assets before AssetLoader initializes
- **Favicon Management** - Updates all favicon `<link>` elements with absolute URLs
- **Environment Agnostic** - Works identically in local development and production

