# Usage in Code

## HTML (Initial Load with Data Attributes)
HTML must use `data-asset-src` and `data-asset-href` attributes instead of direct `src` or `href` attributes. AssetLoader will parse these and inject the absolute URLs on initialization:

```html
<!-- Images: Use data-asset-src attribute -->
<img data-asset-src="../../01__Assets__NaApps__CommonAssets/NaApps__CommonGraphics/NaBrandGraphic__CompanyLogo__w2048xh500px__.png" 
     alt="Company Logo">
<!-- AssetLoader parses data-asset-src, generates absolute URL, sets src attribute -->

<!-- Favicons: Use data-asset-href attribute -->
<link rel="icon" 
      data-asset-href="../../01__Assets__NaApps__CommonAssets/NaApps__CommonIcons/CommonIcon__NaFavicon__ICO-h32px.ico">
<!-- AssetLoader parses data-asset-href, generates absolute URL, sets href attribute -->
```

**Critical:** The browser will not attempt to load assets until AssetLoader injects the real URLs, preventing 404 errors on GitHub Pages.

## CSS (Dynamic Loading)
Fonts are loaded dynamically by AssetLoader - **do not** use `@font-face` in CSS files:
```css
/* -----
 * REGION | Font Face Declarations
 * ----- */

    /* Fonts are dynamically loaded by CommonUtils__AssetLoader__.js */
    /* This ensures absolute URLs work correctly on GitHub Pages */

/* endregion ---- */
```

## JavaScript (Runtime Usage)
Use AssetLoader API for runtime asset references in dynamically generated content:
```javascript
const assetLoader = window.NaProjectAdmin.AssetLoader;
const logoUrl = assetLoader.getAssetUrl('GRAPHICS', 'NaBrandGraphic__CompanyLogo__w2048xh500px__.png');

// Use in dynamic content (QuotationRenderer, TermsRenderer, etc.)
return `<img src="${logoUrl}" alt="Company Logo">`;
```

**Example from QuotationRenderer:**
```javascript
// Get company logo using AssetLoader
const logoUrl = window.NaProjectAdmin.AssetLoader.getAssetUrl(
    'GRAPHICS', 
    'NaBrandGraphic__CompanyLogo__w2048xh500px__.png'
);

// Use in rendered HTML
html += `<img src="${logoUrl}" alt="Noble Architecture" class="quotation-logo">`;
```

