# Rules

## ALWAYS
- Use `data-asset-src` attribute in HTML for images (not `src`)
- Use `data-asset-href` attribute in HTML for links/favicons (not `href`)
- Use `AssetLoader.getAssetUrl()` for JavaScript runtime asset references
- Reference existing centralized assets only
- Include full filename with extension
- Let AssetLoader handle URL resolution and path calculation
- Fonts are loaded automatically by AssetLoader at initialization

## NEVER
- Use direct `src` or `href` attributes for common assets in HTML
- Hardcode absolute URLs in code
- Use relative paths in JavaScript (use AssetLoader API instead)
- Add `@font-face` rules to CSS files (handled by AssetLoader)
- Duplicate Common Assets into app directories
- Modify assets at runtime (read-only)
- Bypass AssetLoader for asset URL calculation

---

# Asset Categories
- **Fonts:** TTF/WOFF/WOFF2 in `NaApps__CommonFonts/`
- **Graphics:** PNG/JPG/SVG brand imagery in `NaApps__CommonGraphics/`
- **Icons:** ICO/PNG/SVG favicons in `NaApps__CommonIcons/`
